WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.525
A model router selects an endpoint using task type, data sensitivity, model capability,

00:00:05.525 --> 00:00:07.620
latency target, availability, and cost.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.040
The eligible set should be determined by policy before performance ranking.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.685
A cloud model that would answer best is not eligible if the prompt contains data that

00:00:14.685 --> 00:00:15.382
cannot leave.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:18.600
Record the route and policy result so behavior can be explained.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.510
Local servers and cloud endpoints may expose similar APIs,

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:26.125
but details differ across streaming, tool calls, context limits, embeddings, error codes,

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.255
and safety behavior.

00:00:27.255 --> 00:00:30.660
Normalize only the features the application uses and test each route.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.635
Model outputs are not interchangeable, so fallback may change quality or format.

00:00:34.635 --> 00:00:37.700
Clients need clear expectations when service is degraded.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.360
Apply rate limits, timeouts, queues,

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.040
and concurrency controls separately for local capacity and paid endpoints.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.080
A local queue should not silently overflow into an expensive cloud route without a cost

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.605
and privacy decision.

00:00:48.605 --> 00:00:52.920
Fallback logic must distinguish capacity failure, authentication failure, policy denial,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.000
and provider outage.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.720
Some failures should stop the request instead of rerouting it.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.515
Protect endpoint credentials and keep them out of prompts, client code, and logs.

00:01:00.515 --> 00:01:04.810
Avoid orchestration that copies entire conversations to every candidate model before

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:06.380
selecting one.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.800
Start with explicit routing rules and a small number of endpoints.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.060
Add automation only when monitoring shows a recurring placement need.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.070
Good orchestration makes data movement, cost,

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:17.480
and failure visible rather than hiding complexity behind one chat box.
